Hi Jim,
Thanks for your help. Yes this is what my data looked like, except that I did have some site covariates. I set up various models, for example:

# Set up competing models
fm1 <- occu(~1 ~ cov1 + cov2, data=umf) # where cov1, cov2 are site covariates
fm2 <- occu(~1 ~ cov1, data=umf)
fm3 <- occu(~cov1 + cov2 ~ cov1 + cov2, data=umf) #This is the full model where I look at                                                                                     the effect of covariates on detection                                                                                     and occupancy
fm4 <- occu(~cov1 ~ cov1 + cov2, data=umf)
# ... So that I have one 'fm' for each possible combination of the effects of each covariate on   both detection probability and occupancy.

Then I ranked models by AICc scores so that I could identify the models in the top candidate set.

Thank you,
Mikey

